<title>CANADA: Rogers Cantel Mobile Q3 net turns to loss.</title>
<headline>Rogers Cantel Mobile Q3 net turns to loss.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	   Loss	C$0.20   Profit	C$0.08</p>
<p> Net	   Loss	18,445   Profit	 7,483</p>
<p> Revs		     286,130		  235,356</p>
<p>	    9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	   Loss	C$0.71   Profit	C$0.05</p>
<p> Net	   Loss	66,869   Profit	 5,121</p>
<p> Revs		     798,677		  652,957</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  93,897		   93,894</p>
<p>(All data above 0000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>Note: Full name is Rogers Cantel Mobile Communications Inc. In the third quarter, Rogers Cantel took a non-recurring, non-cash charge of C$16.7 million for the first generation of Time Division Multiple Access digital handsets to their net realizable value. The company also took a non-recurring cash charge of C$3.6 million for exit costs related to the closing of corporate store operations.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
